// "Part of the stolen life flows back to mend your own wounds" -- a plain
// self-heal-on-hit rider, delivered with `CombatEffect::Lifesteal(f32)`
// (common/src/combat.rs), which always credits the health change to the
// *attacker* regardless of what/who was hit (see its resolution arms: `if
// let Some(attacker_entity) = attacker...`). Already real and shipped on a
// `BasicBeam` via the same-named `damage_effect` field
// (hemomancy/exsanguinate.ron's `damage_effect: Some(Lifesteal(0.3))`);
// `MeleeConstructor` carries an identical `damage_effect: Option<CombatEffect>`
// field that attaches to the normal `OutOfGroup` damage attack the same way
// (`damage.with_effect(damage_effect)` in common/src/comp/melee.rs) -- no
// `attack_effect`/`attack_effect_target` override needed, unlike the
// touch-ally spells elsewhere in this folder, since vampiric_touch hits a
// foe, not an ally.
//
// `MeleeConstructorKind::Stab` has no `damage_kind` field of its own (see
// inflict_wounds.ron/spare_the_dying.ron in this folder, both flavored as
// necrotic/radiant melee hits with no such field either) -- the sheet's
// `damage_type: Necrotic` is kept as flavor/i18n only, same as those
// siblings.
BasicMelee(
    energy_cost: 40.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    swing_duration: 0.1,
    hit_timing: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    melee_constructor: (
        kind: Stab(damage: 24, poise: 5, knockback: 0, energy_regen: 0),
        range: 3.0,
        angle: 20.0,
        damage_effect: Some(Lifesteal(0.35)),
    ),
    meta: (school: Some(Necromancy), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
